{
  "title": "Pupilfirst LMS \u2014 edtech (959\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Pupilfirst LMS\nDomain: edtech | Scale: medium | Stars: 959\nProblem: Provides an open-source Learning Management System designed for asynchronous online education, where students learn through task-based workflows, expert feedback, iterative improvement, and peer collaboration rather than passive content consumption.\nTarget users: Educational institutions, Online schools and academies, Course creators and instructors, Students in asynchronous learning environments\nCore features: Task-based learning with iterative feedback loop; Personalized feedback from domain experts; Community interaction and peer learning; Asynchronous course management; Student progress tracking and assessment; Markdown-based content with rich formatting support; Multi-language support (i18n)\nIntegrations: GraphQL API, Markdown processing (markdown-it with multiple plugins), Email/notification system (PNotify), File storage and export (FileSaver, CSV/Papa Parse), QR code generation\nTech stack: ReScript with React 16, React-DOM, ReScript-React bindings + Ruby on Rails with GraphQL + Unknown (likely PostgreSQL based on Rails conventions) + Docker support (Dockerfile present), Node 18.x, Lerna monorepo\nKey libraries: ReScript (10.1.4), @rescript/react, @reasonml-community/graphql-ppx, Rails 7.0.8, markdown-it with plugins, date-fns, fuse.js (fuzzy search), dompurify, react-datepicker, react-helmet\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Uses ReScript/ReasonML for frontend type safety and compiled-to-JavaScript approach rather than TypeScript, indicating emphasis on correctness and functional programming paradigms\n- Implements GraphQL as primary API layer between Rails backend and ReScript frontend, enabling flexible client-side queries and strong schema validation\n- Monorepo structure with Lerna workspaces for frontend packages suggests modular component architecture while maintaining single codebase for coordinated updates\n- Rich markdown processing pipeline with 11+ markdown-it plugins indicates sophisticated content rendering for educational materials (task descriptions, feedback, collaborative notes)",
